      "writtenOn": "2022-03-21T19:18:18Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "As I think about this more, the Zephyr model for having multiple drivers query a GPIO input is to register a GPIO interrupt callback.  The GPIO API manages a singly linked list of callback handlers.\n\nThat seems pretty heavyweight for this.  For now if you want the pin name, and you don\u0027t want to run afoul of needing to call `gpio_pin_configure_dt()`, you could call this property \"power-good-pin\".  You\u0027ll still extract the GPIO \u0027struct device *` pointer an the GPIO pin number.  Look at the gpio_int.c shim driver as an example.\n\nhttps://chromium.googlesource.com/chromiumos/platform/ec/+/82e218b9/zephyr/shim/src/gpio_int.c#74\n\nOur long term GPIO strategy still needs clarity.  This will also need adapt once Nuvoton and ITE switch from using pinmux drivers to pinctrl drivers.",
      "parentUuid": "bff8d210_7df520b1",
